          <tr>
            <td style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:28px 32px;
                       font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:#212121;">

              <p>Hello fellow hams,</p>

              <p>
                Our first fox hunt of the 2026 season is coming up
                in two weeks. Join us for an on-foot ARDF practice
                hunt at
                <strong>Flaming Geyser State Park</strong> in
                Auburn &mdash; 480+ acres of Green River valley
                terrain with wooded trails and natural multipath
                challenges that make for an excellent introductory
                hunt.
              </p>

              <p>
                This is a great event for first-time hunters.
                Mentors will be on site, and loaner equipment
                (handheld radio and tape-measure Yagi antenna) is
                available at no cost. All license classes are
                welcome.
              </p>

              <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:24px 0 8px;">
                Event Details
              </h3>
              <table width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"
                     border="0"
                     style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.9;">
                <tr>
                  <td width="140"
                      style="color:#555555;vertical-align:top;">
                    Date &amp; Time:
                  </td>
                  <td style="vertical-align:top;">
                    <strong>Sunday, July 19, 2026</strong>
                    (tentative), Noon &ndash; 2:30&nbsp;PM
                  </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td style="color:#555555;vertical-align:top;">
                    Location:
                  </td>
                  <td style="vertical-align:top;">
                    <strong>Flaming Geyser State Park</strong><br>
                    23700 SE Flaming Geyser Rd,
                    Auburn, WA&nbsp;98092
                  </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td style="color:#555555;vertical-align:top;">
                    Frequency:
                  </td>
                  <td style="vertical-align:top;">
                    <strong>147.42&nbsp;MHz simplex</strong>
                    (callsign K7LED)
                  </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td style="color:#555555;vertical-align:top;">
                    Parking:
                  </td>
                  <td style="vertical-align:top;">
                    <strong>Discover Pass required</strong> per
                    vehicle ($11.50 day-use or $35 annual).
                    Carpools encouraged &mdash; contact the group
                    to coordinate rides.
                  </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td style="color:#555555;vertical-align:top;">
                    Hunt type:
                  </td>
                  <td style="vertical-align:top;">
                    Single milliwatt fox, on-foot ARDF
                  </td>
                </tr>
              </table>

              <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:24px 0 8px;">
                What to Bring
              </h3>
              <ul style="margin:8px 0;padding-left:20px;">
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  <strong>Handheld transceiver</strong> programmed
                  to 147.42&nbsp;MHz &mdash; or borrow one at
                  the event
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  <strong>Tape-measure Yagi antenna</strong>
                  &mdash; or borrow one at the event
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  Switched step attenuator (for close-in hunting)
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  <strong>Discover Pass</strong> or cash
                  ($11.50) for day-use parking
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  Comfortable walking shoes; trail terrain
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  Water and a snack; sun protection
                </li>
              </ul>

              <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:24px 0 8px;">
                About the Venue
              </h3>
              <p>
                Flaming Geyser State Park sits along the Green
                River in Auburn with a mix of open meadows and
                wooded riverside trails. The forested sections
                create realistic signal multipath &mdash; exactly
                the kind of challenge that sharpens your
                direction-finding skills. Parking is along the
                main entrance road near the picnic shelters.
              </p>

              <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:24px 0 8px;">
                RSVP &amp; Questions
              </h3>
              <p>
                An RSVP is helpful so we can plan the right number
                of loaner radios. Reply to this message or contact
                <strong>Tom Sayles, KE4HET</strong> at
                [TOM-EMAIL].
              </p>

              <p>
                We look forward to seeing you in the field. 73
                de KE4HET
              </p>

